    },
    {
      "id": "n5_b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 392,
      "y": 1034,
      "width": 766,
      "height": 136,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2058577411,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 318429187,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.  The ECR pull uses ecr_image_puller_role, NOT the service's\nprincipal_arn. They are different ARNs. Granting the wrong one fails\nwith NO error anywhere: no container, no logs, the deployment just\nreports Canceled.\n\n2.  Lightsail READ actions cannot be resource-scoped - they need\nResource: *. Create-deployment DOES accept an ARN, which is what\nmakes it confusing: the deploy succeeds, only polling is denied.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.  The ECR pull uses ecr_image_puller_role, NOT the service's\nprincipal_arn. They are different ARNs. Granting the wrong one fails\nwith NO error anywhere: no container, no logs, the deployment just\nreports Canceled.\n\n2.  Lightsail READ actions cannot be resource-scoped - they need\nResource: *. Create-deployment DOES accept an ARN, which is what\nmakes it confusing: the deploy succeeds, only polling is denied.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "n6",
